# Anti-fascist frames: Eco 1995, Stanley 2018, Beauvoir, Deleuze-Guattari, Foucault, Fisher, Lacan, Grok 2025. See philosophy/ANTIFASCISM.md and core/ontology/SOURCES.md.
# A detector of rhetoric is never labelled checked. It flags text for a person to judge. It is never a verdict on a person or group.
check "python3 -I philosophy/antifascism.py"
check "python3 -I philosophy/rhizome.py"
kripke dom = worlds 3 rel [(0,0), (0,1), (0,2), (1,1), (2,2), (1,2)]
claim invalid dom "p -> []<>p"
frame "Beauvoir, the serious man and oppression, Pour une morale de l'ambiguite 1947 (not re-read); fascism as refusal of reciprocity is analogy (reading), not checked" reading "Kripke fact only: on every frame on 2..4 worlds, at every world that reaches all and is reached by none, B fails (philosophy/antifascism.py part A, 66064 frames)" -> 3 label checked-finite reach 2 cost 80
frame "Beauvoir, as above; smallest case" reading "Kripke fact only: world 0 reaches 0,1,2 and is reached by none; B is invalid, countermodel printed" -> 6 label checked-finite reach 1 cost 40
frame "Deleuze and Guattari, L'Anti-Oedipe 1972; Foucault, preface to Anti-Oedipus 1977 (not re-read); microfascism as a single critical centre is analogy (reading), not checked" reading "graph fact only: a connected graph whose every edge touches one vertex and is critical is exactly the star; a connected graph is a tree iff every edge is critical (rhizome.py)" -> 3 label checked-finite reach 2 cost 80
frame "Deleuze and Guattari, the rhizome against the arborescent centre (philosophy/rhizome.py)" reading "graph fact only: bridgeless connected graphs have no critical part; trees have only critical parts" -> 4 label checked-finite reach 1 cost 40
frame "Fisher, Capitalist Realism 2009 (not re-read); no alternative as an absorbing class is analogy (reading), not checked" reading "chain fact only: math/transit/social.py part a, absorption probability 1 into closed classes" -> none label open reach 1 cost 80
frame "Lacan, paranoia and the master signifier (not re-read); Eco's obsession with a plot as meaning anchored to one persecutor" reading "reading only; no structure checked" -> none label open reach 1 cost 120
frame "Eco, Ur-Fascism 1995 (Il fascismo eterno) and Stanley, How Fascism Works 2018 (not re-read); feature names paraphrased" reading "keyword detector, tested on 20 synthetic sentences: precision 0.91, recall 1.00, false-positive rate 0.10; crude; flags for human review only; never checked" -> 3 label tested reach 2 cost 80
frame "Grok incidents 2025 (NPR 2025-07-09; TechCrunch 2025-05-14, 2025-07-12; relayed, not re-read); topic intrusion as aberrant salience, Kapur 2003" reading "reading only: filter removal as removed reality testing; one upstream change as a single critical part (cf. star fact)" -> none label open reach 1 cost 120
